WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.949
One sale is a start, not long-term proof.

00:00:02.949 --> 00:00:05.161
Keep learning after the first dollar.

00:00:05.161 --> 00:00:08.480
This lesson is about one sale ≠ long-term proof.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.323
Keep learning after first dollar.

00:00:10.323 --> 00:00:12.904
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:12.904 --> 00:00:16.590
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:22.120
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:26.176
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:26.176 --> 00:00:30.600
Stay practical: list next three experiments before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:35.130
Do not freeze the offer forever because one person paid once.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.809
Remember the objective: list next three experiments.

00:00:37.809 --> 00:00:42.019
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:42.019 --> 00:00:46.612
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:50.821
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:50.821 --> 00:00:55.414
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:55.414 --> 00:00:58.093
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:58.093 --> 00:00:59.624
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:59.944 --> 00:01:04.235
List the next three experiments: who else, what message, what tweak.

